# READ-FIELD-CLOSURE (T7), an explicit path addresses the graph: model's own `node\cnt` in the node w reads the copy of
# its lexical parent made at the merge, 7 -- not the root's binding 9 or the unit's cell 11 (docs #dynamic: explicit
# access is not replaced by the current call's dynamic value).  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
int: cnt 7
fn: model (int: y) int
    return: node\cnt
fn: wrap (int: k) fn: () int
    return: merge(y: k; model)
sub: poke ()
    node\cnt: 11
@: w wrap(5)
cnt: 9
poke()
int: result w()
int: ok 7
if: result != 7
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
